            </span>
            <h4 class="font-marcellus text-base sm:text-lg text-[#06192e] uppercase tracking-wide">
              What Is the Difference Between a Sunset Cruise and a Day Cruise in Poovar?
            </h4>
            <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-gray-700 leading-relaxed font-light">
              A day cruise shows the backwaters in bright light, while a sunset cruise runs near dusk, with softer light, cooler air and sky colours over the water.
            </p>
            <p class="text-xs text-gray-600 leading-relaxed font-light">
              Choose a day cruise to see the mangroves and birds clearly. Choose the sunset cruise for photos and a calmer, cooler ride.
            </p>
          </div>

          <!-- Question 2: How Long Is the Poovar Sunset Cruise? -->
          <div class="space-y-3 pt-6 lg:pt-0 lg:px-4">
            <span class="font-marcellus text-3xl sm:text-4xl text-[#b19d7f] font-bold block">
              02
            </span>
            <h4 class="font-marcellus text-base sm:text-lg text-[#06192e] uppercase tracking-wide">
              How Long Is the Poovar Sunset Cruise?
            </h4>
            <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-gray-700 leading-relaxed font-light">
              The Poovar Boat Tour sunset cruise runs from about 5:00 PM to 6:30 PM, which is about 1.5 hours on the water. Tell us your date and we will confirm the start time, so you are on the water at sunset.
            </p>
            <div class="pt-1 text-[11px] font-mono font-bold text-[#b19d7f] uppercase tracking-wider">
              ~1.5 Hours &bull; Departs ~5:00 PM
            </div>
          </div>

          <!-- Question 3: Best Time of Day for a Boat Ride -->
          <div class="space-y-3 pt-6 lg:pt-0 lg:px-4">
            <span class="font-marcellus text-3xl sm:text-4xl text-[#b19d7f] font-bold block">
              03
            </span>
            <h4 class="font-marcellus text-base sm:text-lg text-[#06192e] uppercase tracking-wide">
              What Is the Best Time of Day for a Poovar Boat Ride?
            </h4>
            <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-gray-700 leading-relaxed font-light">
              Early morning and late afternoon are the best times for a Poovar boat ride, because the heat is lower, the water is calm and the light is good for photos.
            </p>
            <p class="text-xs text-gray-600 leading-relaxed font-light">
              Morning is also best for bird watching, because many birds are active early in the day.
            </p>
          </div>

          <!-- Question 4: What Is the Poovar Estuary? -->
          <div class="space-y-3 pt-6 lg:pt-0 lg:px-4">
            <span class="font-marcellus text-3xl sm:text-4xl text-[#b19d7f] font-bold block">
              04
            </span>
            <h4 class="font-marcellus text-base sm:text-lg text-[#06192e] uppercase tracking-wide">
              What Is the Poovar Estuary?
            </h4>
            <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-gray-700 leading-relaxed font-light">
              The Poovar estuary is the place where the Neyyar River meets the Arabian Sea. The boat ride goes through this area, so you see river water and sea together.
            </p>
            <div class="pt-1 text-[11px] font-mono font-bold text-[#b19d7f] uppercase tracking-wider">
              River Meets Sea Sanctuary
            </div>
          </div>

          <!-- Question 5: What Are the Mangroves in Poovar? -->
          <div class="space-y-3 pt-6 lg:pt-0 lg:px-4">
            <span class="font-marcellus text-3xl sm:text-4xl text-[#b19d7f] font-bold block">
              05
            </span>
            <h4 class="font-marcellus text-base sm:text-lg text-[#06192e] uppercase tracking-wide">
              What Are the Mangroves in Poovar?
            </h4>
            <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-gray-700 leading-relaxed font-light">
              Mangroves are salt-tolerant trees that grow along the banks of the backwaters. Their roots shelter fish and birds, and the boat passes close to them.
            </p>
            <div class="pt-1 text-[11px] font-mono font-bold text-[#b19d7f] uppercase tracking-wider">
              Protected Root Canals
            </div>
          </div>

